      "title": "Use banner image if it's been chosen",
      "user_name": "Trey Pendragon",
      "comments": [
        {
          "user_name": "Trey Pendragon",
          "updated_at": "2026-05-29T22:29:21",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/pulibrary/dpul-collections/pull/1236#issuecomment-4580339951",
          "body": "> 2\\. I am not sad about the banner link to the item going away. I think we should provide a link to the item, but we should do it via an accurate citation + link under the image.  That would be better UX and would model the preferred citations for users and suggest they use it for research/transformative uses.\r\n\r\nSure, my motivation was I wanted to see the item with the cute cat, but I had no way to do so."
        }
